IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `aia-core`
IMPORT `aia-timeline`

-- P6-art-51-52: Chapter V Section 1, Articles 51 and 52, the classification of a general-purpose AI model as one with systemic risk, and the procedure
-- (Regulation (EU) 2024/1689 as amended by Regulation (EU) 2026/1744; the consolidated text of 27.7.2026 is a rendering with no legal effect).
-- Neither Article was changed by the Omnibus: one text, no version split in this module.
-- Layer 1: the law, objectively. Every function takes `the date asked` first. NOTHING is "not covered" (NOTHING-kind); JUST FALSE is the text's own no (FALSE-kind);
-- JUST TRUE says the paragraph's rule, duty or power arises on the facts.
-- Chapter V is in the provision group `Notified bodies, GPAI, governance, penalties and Art 78`, which applies from 2 August 2025 (Art 113 third paragraph, point (b)).
-- Article 111(3) gives a provider of a general-purpose AI model placed on the market before 2 August 2025 until 2 August 2027 to comply with "the obligations laid down in this Regulation":
-- read as delaying the obligations of a provider (fork F-111-3-scope: Articles 52(1), 53, 54 and 55, not the classification of Article 51, not a power of the Commission, not Article 56).
-- A model is not an AI system: every function here passes the core's route and placement-date constants to the keel's applicability function, never a system's.
-- The seat computes a defined term with the keel's Article 3 function and passes the answer in as a BOOLEAN input named for the definition.

§ `Chapter V: when it applies`

-- The group applies from 2 August 2025.
GIVEN `the date asked` IS A DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Art 51 the group applies on the date asked` MEANS
    `Art 113 the provision group applies` `Notified bodies, GPAI, governance, penalties and Art 78` `the date asked` `the route to pass when no AI system is in question` `the date to pass when no AI system is in question` FALSE

-- Article 111(3), as it bears on the duties of a provider of a general-purpose AI model: a model placed on the market before 2 August 2025 has until 2 August 2027.
-- True from the day the group applies for a model placed on or after 2 August 2025; from 2 August 2027 for an earlier one; never before the group applies.
-- src:1625 | 3. Providers of general-purpose AI models that have been placed on the market before 2 August 2025 shall take the necessary steps in order to comply with the obligations laid down in this Regulation by 2 August 2027.
@ref Art 111(3), as it bears on the obligations of Chapter V (src:1625)
GIVEN `the date asked` IS A DATE
      `the model` IS AN `AI model`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Art 51 the time to comply has come for the provider of the model on the date asked` MEANS
        `Art 51 the group applies on the date asked` `the date asked`
    AND CONSIDER `Art 111(3) the date by which the provider of a general-purpose AI model already on the market must comply` `the date asked` (`the model`'s `date placed on the market`)
        WHEN NOTHING THEN TRUE
        WHEN JUST `the deadline` THEN `the date asked` AT LEAST `the deadline`

-- The gate that every duty of a provider of a general-purpose AI model in Chapter V (Articles 53 to 55 and Annexes XI and XII) passes through:
-- Chapter V applies, the model is a general-purpose AI model, and the time of Art 111(3) has come. JUST TRUE says the provider is bound; NOTHING says the text does not bind it yet or at all.
GIVEN `the date asked` IS A DATE
      `the model` IS AN `AI model`
      `the model is a general-purpose AI model` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Art 51 the obligations of the provider of the model are owed on the date asked` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT (`Art 51 the group applies on the date asked` `the date asked`)
            THEN NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): Chapter V applies from the date Art 113 gives
        IF NOT `the model is a general-purpose AI model`
            THEN NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the obligations are those of "providers of general-purpose AI models"
        IF NOT (`Art 51 the time to comply has come for the provider of the model on the date asked` `the date asked` `the model`)
            THEN NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): Art 111(3) gives a provider of a model placed on the market before 2 August 2025 until 2 August 2027
        OTHERWISE JUST TRUE

-- The Commission, the AI Office and the Board are parties of the rules of Chapter V that address them. They have no seat: the seat layer asks what their rules mean to the five seats.
DECLARE `Art 51 official` IS ONE OF
    `Art 51 the Commission`
    `Art 51 the AI Office`
    `Art 51 the Board`

DECLARE `Art 51 act` IS ONE OF
    `Art 51(3) adopt delegated acts under Article 97 to amend the thresholds, and to supplement benchmarks and indicators`

DECLARE `Art 52 act` IS ONE OF
    `Art 52(1) notify the Commission that the model meets the condition referred to in Article 51(1), point (a)`
    `Art 52(3) reject the arguments submitted by the provider`
    `Art 52(6) publish the list of general-purpose AI models with systemic risk and keep it up to date`

§ `Article 51(2): the presumption of high impact capabilities (the threshold is ten to the power twenty-five)`

-- "when the cumulative amount of computation used for its training measured in floating point operations is greater than 10^25".
-- The threshold is the exact literal, not EXPONENT (the formulas sidecar: EXPONENT 10 25 is wrong by about 9 x 10^8 on the main build).
-- "greater than": a model trained with exactly 10^25 operations is not presumed.
`Art 51(2) the threshold of floating-point operations` MEANS 10_000_000_000_000_000_000_000_000

-- src:772 | 2. A general-purpose AI model shall be presumed to have high impact capabilities pursuant to paragraph 1, point (a), when the cumulative amount of computation used for its training measured in floating point operations is greater than 10^25.
@ref Art 51(2) (src:772)
GIVEN `the date asked` IS A DATE
      `the model` IS AN `AI model`
      `the model is a general-purpose AI model` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Art 51(2) the model is presumed to have high impact capabilities` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT (`Art 51 the group applies on the date asked` `the date asked`)
            THEN NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): Chapter V applies from the date Art 113 gives
        IF NOT `the model is a general-purpose AI model`
            THEN NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "A general-purpose AI model shall be presumed"
        IF `the model`'s `cumulative compute used for its training, in floating-point operations` GREATER THAN `Art 51(2) the threshold of floating-point operations`
            THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE JUST FALSE  -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "shall be presumed ... when the cumulative amount of computation ... is greater than 10^25" (a "when" condition counts as "where": it fails, so no presumption arises; the model can still meet Article 51(1)(a) by evaluation)

§ `Article 51(1): classification as a general-purpose AI model with systemic risk`

-- Point (a): "it has high impact capabilities evaluated on the basis of appropriate technical tools and methodologies, including indicators and benchmarks".
-- Article 51(2) presumes this when the compute exceeds the threshold, so the point is met by the evaluation or by the presumption (fork F-51-1-a-presumption: the presumption can be rebutted
-- under Article 52(2), but the text does not say what follows when the Commission accepts the arguments: see NOTES.md, what the text does not answer).
-- src:769 | 1. A general-purpose AI model shall be classified as a general-purpose AI model with systemic risk if it meets any of the following conditions:
-- src:770 | (a) it has high impact capabilities evaluated on the basis of appropriate technical tools and methodologies, including indicators and benchmarks;
@ref Art 51(1)(a) (src:769-770)
GIVEN `the date asked` IS A DATE
      `the model` IS AN `AI model`
      `the model is a general-purpose AI model` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the model has high impact capabilities evaluated on the basis of appropriate technical tools and methodologies, including indicators and benchmarks` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Art 51(1)(a) the model meets the condition of high impact capabilities` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT (`Art 51 the group applies on the date asked` `the date asked`)
            THEN NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): Chapter V applies from the date Art 113 gives
        IF NOT `the model is a general-purpose AI model`
            THEN NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "A general-purpose AI model shall be classified"
        IF     `the model has high impact capabilities evaluated on the basis of appropriate technical tools and methodologies, including indicators and benchmarks`
            OR (`Art 51(2) the model is presumed to have high impact capabilities` `the date asked` `the model` `the model is a general-purpose AI model` EQUALS JUST TRUE)
            THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE JUST FALSE  -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "if it meets any of the following conditions: (a) it has high impact capabilities evaluated ..." (a failed "if" counts as the text's no, clause by clause)

-- Point (b): "based on a decision of the Commission, ex officio or following a qualified alert from the scientific panel, it has capabilities or an impact equivalent to those set out in
-- point (a) having regard to the criteria set out in Annex XIII". The decision is the designation of Article 52(4) and, for a model not notified, of Article 52(1), third sentence.
-- src:771 | (b) based on a decision of the Commission, ex officio or following a qualified alert from the scientific panel, it has capabilities or an impact equivalent to those set out in point (a) having regard to the criteria set out in Annex XIII.
@ref Art 51(1)(b) (src:771)
GIVEN `the date asked` IS A DATE
      `the model is a general-purpose AI model` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the Commission has decided, ex officio or following a qualified alert from the scientific panel, that the model has capabilities or an impact equivalent to those set out in point (a), having regard to the criteria set out in Annex XIII` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Art 51(1)(b) the model meets the condition of a decision of the Commission` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT (`Art 51 the group applies on the date asked` `the date asked`)
            THEN NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): Chapter V applies from the date Art 113 gives
        IF NOT `the model is a general-purpose AI model`
            THEN NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "A general-purpose AI model shall be classified"
        IF `the Commission has decided, ex officio or following a qualified alert from the scientific panel, that the model has capabilities or an impact equivalent to those set out in point (a), having regard to the criteria set out in Annex XIII`
            THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE JUST FALSE  -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "if it meets any of the following conditions: ... (b) based on a decision of the Commission ..." (a failed "if" counts as the text's no, clause by clause)

-- src:769 | 1. A general-purpose AI model shall be classified as a general-purpose AI model with systemic risk if it meets any of the following conditions:
@ref Art 51(1) (src:769)
GIVEN `the date asked` IS A DATE
      `the model` IS AN `AI model`
      `the model is a general-purpose AI model` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the model has high impact capabilities evaluated on the basis of appropriate technical tools and methodologies, including indicators and benchmarks` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the Commission has decided, ex officio or following a qualified alert from the scientific panel, that the model has capabilities or an impact equivalent to those set out in point (a), having regard to the criteria set out in Annex XIII` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Art 51(1) the model is classified as a general-purpose AI model with systemic risk` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT (`Art 51 the group applies on the date asked` `the date asked`)
            THEN NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): Chapter V applies from the date Art 113 gives
        IF NOT `the model is a general-purpose AI model`
            THEN NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "A general-purpose AI model shall be classified"
        IF     (`Art 51(1)(a) the model meets the condition of high impact capabilities` `the date asked` `the model` `the model is a general-purpose AI model` `the model has high impact capabilities evaluated on the basis of appropriate technical tools and methodologies, including indicators and benchmarks` EQUALS JUST TRUE)
            OR (`Art 51(1)(b) the model meets the condition of a decision of the Commission` `the date asked` `the model is a general-purpose AI model` `the Commission has decided, ex officio or following a qualified alert from the scientific panel, that the model has capabilities or an impact equivalent to those set out in point (a), having regard to the criteria set out in Annex XIII` EQUALS JUST TRUE)
            THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE JUST FALSE  -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "shall be classified ... if it meets any of the following conditions" (a failed "if" counts as the text's no)

-- The seam S5 of PLAN.md section 4: the answer the Articles that ask "is the model one with systemic risk" (Articles 55, 88 to 94, 101) take as an input.
-- A BOOLEAN: NOTHING and JUST FALSE both read FALSE here, which is how the asking Articles use it (NOTES.md, Seams).
@ref Art 51(1) (the seam S5)
GIVEN `the date asked` IS A DATE
      `the model` IS AN `AI model`
      `the model is a general-purpose AI model` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the model has high impact capabilities evaluated on the basis of appropriate technical tools and methodologies, including indicators and benchmarks` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the Commission has decided, ex officio or following a qualified alert from the scientific panel, that the model has capabilities or an impact equivalent to those set out in point (a), having regard to the criteria set out in Annex XIII` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Art 51 the general-purpose AI model is classified as a general-purpose AI model with systemic risk under Article 51` MEANS
    `Art 51(1) the model is classified as a general-purpose AI model with systemic risk` `the date asked` `the model` `the model is a general-purpose AI model` `the model has high impact capabilities evaluated on the basis of appropriate technical tools and methodologies, including indicators and benchmarks` `the Commission has decided, ex officio or following a qualified alert from the scientific panel, that the model has capabilities or an impact equivalent to those set out in point (a), having regard to the criteria set out in Annex XIII` EQUALS JUST TRUE

§ `Article 51(3): delegated acts on the thresholds`

-- "The Commission shall adopt delegated acts ... when necessary for these thresholds to reflect the state of the art": a duty of the Commission, gated by "when necessary".
-- src:773 | 3. The Commission shall adopt delegated acts in accordance with Article 97 to amend the thresholds listed in paragraphs 1 and 2 of this Article, as well as to supplement benchmarks and indicators in light of evolving technological developments, such as algorithmic improvements or increased hardware efficiency, when necessary, for these thresholds to reflect the state of the art.
@ref Art 51(3) (src:773)
GIVEN `the date asked` IS A DATE
      `it is necessary for the thresholds to reflect the state of the art` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Art 51(3) the Commission must adopt delegated acts to amend the thresholds and to supplement benchmarks and indicators` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT (`Art 51 the group applies on the date asked` `the date asked`)
            THEN NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): Chapter V applies from the date Art 113 gives
        IF `it is necessary for the thresholds to reflect the state of the art`
            THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE JUST FALSE  -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "when necessary for these thresholds to reflect the state of the art" (a "when" condition counts as "where": it fails, so the duty does not arise)

@ref Art 51(3) (the duty; no time limit and no consequence in the text)
GIVEN `the date asked` IS A DATE
      `it is necessary for the thresholds to reflect the state of the art` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A DEONTIC `Art 51 official` `Art 51 act`
`Art 51(3) the Commission's duty to adopt delegated acts` MEANS
    IF `Art 51(3) the Commission must adopt delegated acts to amend the thresholds and to supplement benchmarks and indicators` `the date asked` `it is necessary for the thresholds to reflect the state of the art` EQUALS JUST TRUE
    THEN PARTY `Art 51 the Commission`
         MUST `Art 51(3) adopt delegated acts under Article 97 to amend the thresholds, and to supplement benchmarks and indicators`
         -- no time limit and no consequence in the text (listed in NOTES.md, Rules with no breach path)
    ELSE FULFILLED  -- nothing is owed on these facts

§ `Article 52(1): the notification`

-- "Where a general-purpose AI model meets the condition referred to in Article 51(1), point (a), the relevant provider shall notify the Commission without delay and in any event within two weeks
-- after that requirement is met or it becomes known that it will be met." A duty of the provider, in the group of Chapter V; Article 111(3) can give a provider of an earlier model until 2 August 2027.
-- src:776 | 1. Where a general-purpose AI model meets the condition referred to in Article 51(1), point (a), the relevant provider shall notify the Commission without delay and in any event within two weeks after that requirement is met or it becomes known that it will be met. That notification shall include the information necessary to demonstrate that the relevant requirement has been met. If the Commission becomes aware of a general-purpose AI model presenting systemic risks of which it has not been notified, it may decide to designate it as a model with systemic risk.
@ref Art 52(1) first sentence (src:776)
GIVEN `the date asked` IS A DATE
      `the model` IS AN `AI model`
      `the model is a general-purpose AI model` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the model meets the condition referred to in Article 51(1), point (a)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Art 52(1) the provider must notify the Commission that the model meets the condition referred to in Article 51(1), point (a)` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT (`Art 51 the group applies on the date asked` `the date asked`)
            THEN NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): Chapter V applies from the date Art 113 gives
        IF NOT `the model is a general-purpose AI model`
            THEN NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "Where a general-purpose AI model meets the condition"
        IF NOT (`Art 51 the time to comply has come for the provider of the model on the date asked` `the date asked` `the model`)
            THEN NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): Art 111(3) gives a provider of a model placed on the market before 2 August 2025 until 2 August 2027
        IF `the model meets the condition referred to in Article 51(1), point (a)`
            THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE JUST FALSE  -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Where a general-purpose AI model meets the condition referred to in Article 51(1), point (a)" (a "where" condition: when it fails the answer is no)

-- The time. Two weeks run from the earlier of the day the requirement is met and the day it becomes known that it will be met (fork F-52-1-start: the text says "or", and the earlier day
-- is the one that serves "without delay"; the other reading runs from the later). "Without delay and in any event within two weeks" is two conditions (fork F-52-1-without-delay).
@ref Art 52(1) first sentence (the time)
GIVEN `the date asked` IS A DATE
      `the model` IS AN `AI model`
      `the model is a general-purpose AI model` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the model meets the condition referred to in Article 51(1), point (a)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the date the requirement is met or, if earlier, the date it becomes known that it will be met` IS A DATE
      `the date the provider notified the Commission` IS A DATE
      `the provider notified the Commission without delay` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Art 52(1) the provider notified the Commission without delay and within two weeks` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `Art 52(1) the provider must notify the Commission that the model meets the condition referred to in Article 51(1), point (a)` `the date asked` `the model` `the model is a general-purpose AI model` `the model meets the condition referred to in Article 51(1), point (a)` EQUALS NOTHING
            THEN NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the duty does not arise on these facts (Chapter V not yet applicable, not a general-purpose AI model, or Art 111(3) time not yet run)
        IF `Art 52(1) the provider must notify the Commission that the model meets the condition referred to in Article 51(1), point (a)` `the date asked` `the model` `the model is a general-purpose AI model` `the model meets the condition referred to in Article 51(1), point (a)` EQUALS JUST FALSE
            THEN JUST FALSE  -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Where a general-purpose AI model meets the condition ..." (the condition is not met: no notification is owed)
        IF `the date the provider notified the Commission` GREATER THAN (`the date the requirement is met or, if earlier, the date it becomes known that it will be met` PLUS 14)
            THEN JUST FALSE  -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "in any event within two weeks after that requirement is met or it becomes known that it will be met"
        IF NOT `the provider notified the Commission without delay`
            THEN JUST FALSE  -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "shall notify the Commission without delay" (a bare "shall" not done, taken case by case)
        OTHERWISE JUST TRUE

@ref Art 52(1) first sentence (the duty)
GIVEN `the date asked` IS A DATE
      `the model` IS AN `AI model`
      `the model is a general-purpose AI model` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the model meets the condition referred to in Article 51(1), point (a)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A DEONTIC Role `Art 52 act`
`Art 52(1) the provider's duty to notify the Commission` MEANS
    IF `Art 52(1) the provider must notify the Commission that the model meets the condition referred to in Article 51(1), point (a)` `the date asked` `the model` `the model is a general-purpose AI model` `the model meets the condition referred to in Article 51(1), point (a)` EQUALS JUST TRUE
    THEN PARTY Provider
         MUST `Art 52(1) notify the Commission that the model meets the condition referred to in Article 51(1), point (a)`
         WITHIN 14
         HENCE FULFILLED
         LEST BREACH BY Provider BECAUSE "the Commission was not notified within two weeks after the requirement was met or it became known that it will be met"
    ELSE FULFILLED  -- nothing is owed on these facts

-- Second sentence: "That notification shall include the information necessary to demonstrate that the relevant requirement has been met."
-- src:776 | 1. Where a general-purpose AI model meets the condition referred to in Article 51(1), point (a), the relevant provider shall notify the Commission without delay and in any event within two weeks after that requirement is met or it becomes known that it will be met. That notification shall include the information necessary to demonstrate that the relevant requirement has been met. If the Commission becomes aware of a general-purpose AI model presenting systemic risks of which it has not been notified, it may decide to designate it as a model with systemic risk.
@ref Art 52(1) second sentence (src:776)
GIVEN `the date asked` IS A DATE
      `the model` IS AN `AI model`
      `the model is a general-purpose AI model` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the model meets the condition referred to in Article 51(1), point (a)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the notification includes the information necessary to demonstrate that the relevant requirement has been met` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Art 52(1) the notification includes the information necessary to demonstrate that the relevant requirement has been met` MEANS
    IF `Art 52(1) the provider must notify the Commission that the model meets the condition referred to in Article 51(1), point (a)` `the date asked` `the model` `the model is a general-purpose AI model` `the model meets the condition referred to in Article 51(1), point (a)` EQUALS JUST TRUE
    THEN JUST `the notification includes the information necessary to demonstrate that the relevant requirement has been met`
         -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "That notification shall include the information necessary to demonstrate that the relevant requirement has been met" (a bare "shall" not done, taken case by case)
    ELSE NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the sentence speaks of the notification the first sentence requires

-- Third sentence: "If the Commission becomes aware of a general-purpose AI model presenting systemic risks of which it has not been notified, it may decide to designate it as a model with systemic risk."
-- A "may" gated by "if": the function is named for a power, so a failed gate is NOTHING (the grant ruling of 2026-11-12; fork F-52-1-if).
-- src:776 | 1. Where a general-purpose AI model meets the condition referred to in Article 51(1), point (a), the relevant provider shall notify the Commission without delay and in any event within two weeks after that requirement is met or it becomes known that it will be met. That notification shall include the information necessary to demonstrate that the relevant requirement has been met. If the Commission becomes aware of a general-purpose AI model presenting systemic risks of which it has not been notified, it may decide to designate it as a model with systemic risk.
@ref Art 52(1) third sentence (src:776)
GIVEN `the date asked` IS A DATE
      `the model is a general-purpose AI model` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the Commission becomes aware of a general-purpose AI model presenting systemic risks` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the Commission has not been notified of that model` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Art 52(1) the Commission may decide to designate the model as a model with systemic risk` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT (`Art 51 the group applies on the date asked` `the date asked`)
            THEN NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): Chapter V applies from the date Art 113 gives
        IF NOT `the model is a general-purpose AI model`
            THEN NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "a general-purpose AI model presenting systemic risks"
        IF `the Commission becomes aware of a general-purpose AI model presenting systemic risks` AND `the Commission has not been notified of that model`
            THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the power is given "If the Commission becomes aware of ... of which it has not been notified"

§ `Article 52(2): arguments that the model does not present systemic risks`

-- "The provider of a general-purpose AI model that meets the condition referred to in Article 51(1), point (a), may present, with its notification, sufficiently substantiated arguments ...".
-- A power of the provider, limited by its own wording to a model that meets the condition and to the arguments presented with the notification: a case outside the limit is NOTHING.
-- The power is not gated by the arguments being substantiated: Article 52(3) judges whether they are (fork F-52-2-sufficient).
-- src:777 | 2. The provider of a general-purpose AI model that meets the condition referred to in Article 51(1), point (a), may present, with its notification, sufficiently substantiated arguments to demonstrate that, exceptionally, although it meets that requirement, the general-purpose AI model does not present, due to its specific characteristics, systemic risks and therefore should not be classified as a general-purpose AI model with systemic risk.
@ref Art 52(2) (src:777)
GIVEN `the date asked` IS A DATE
      `the model is a general-purpose AI model` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the model meets the condition referred to in Article 51(1), point (a)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the arguments are presented with the notification` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Art 52(2) the provider may present arguments that the model does not present systemic risks` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT (`Art 51 the group applies on the date asked` `the date asked`)
            THEN NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): Chapter V applies from the date Art 113 gives
        IF NOT `the model is a general-purpose AI model`
            THEN NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "The provider of a general-purpose AI model"
        IF `the model meets the condition referred to in Article 51(1), point (a)` AND `the arguments are presented with the notification`
            THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the power is given to a provider whose model meets the condition, to present arguments "with its notification"

§ `Article 52(3): rejecting the arguments`

-- "Where the Commission concludes that the arguments ... are not sufficiently substantiated and the relevant provider was not able to demonstrate that the model does not present ... systemic risks,
-- it shall reject those arguments, and the general-purpose AI model shall be considered to be a general-purpose AI model with systemic risk."
-- What follows when the Commission is satisfied is not in the text (NOTES.md, what the text does not answer).
-- src:778 | 3. Where the Commission concludes that the arguments submitted pursuant to paragraph 2 are not sufficiently substantiated and the relevant provider was not able to demonstrate that the general-purpose AI model does not present, due to its specific characteristics, systemic risks, it shall reject those arguments, and the general-purpose AI model shall be considered to be a general-purpose AI model with systemic risk.
@ref Art 52(3) (src:778)
GIVEN `the date asked` IS A DATE
      `the model is a general-purpose AI model` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the Commission concludes that the arguments submitted pursuant to paragraph 2 are not sufficiently substantiated` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the relevant provider was not able to demonstrate that the model does not present, due to its specific characteristics, systemic risks` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Art 52(3) the Commission must reject the arguments submitted pursuant to paragraph 2` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT (`Art 51 the group applies on the date asked` `the date asked`)
            THEN NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): Chapter V applies from the date Art 113 gives
        IF NOT `the model is a general-purpose AI model`
            THEN NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "the general-purpose AI model"
        IF `the Commission concludes that the arguments submitted pursuant to paragraph 2 are not sufficiently substantiated` AND `the relevant provider was not able to demonstrate that the model does not present, due to its specific characteristics, systemic risks`
            THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE JUST FALSE  -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Where the Commission concludes that the arguments ... are not sufficiently substantiated and the relevant provider was not able to demonstrate ..." (a "where" condition: when it fails the answer is no)

