GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Art 52(4) the Commission may adopt delegated acts to amend Annex XIII by specifying and updating the criteria` MEANS
    IF `Art 51 the group applies on the date asked` `the date asked`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): Chapter V applies from the date Art 113 gives

§ `Article 52(5): reassessment of a designation`

-- "Upon a reasoned request of a provider whose model has been designated ... pursuant to paragraph 4, the Commission shall take the request into account and may decide to reassess ...".
-- Two functions, one for the duty and one for the power; both are gated by "Upon", which counts as "where": a failed gate is JUST FALSE for both (split site (ii), fork F-52-5-upon).
-- A model that has not been designated is outside the sentence: NOTHING.
-- src:781 | 5. Upon a reasoned request of a provider whose model has been designated as a general-purpose AI model with systemic risk pursuant to paragraph 4, the Commission shall take the request into account and may decide to reassess whether the general-purpose AI model can still be considered to present systemic risks on the basis of the criteria set out in Annex XIII. Such a request shall contain objective, detailed and new reasons that have arisen since the designation decision. Providers may request reassessment at the earliest six months after the designation decision. Where the Commission, following its reassessment, decides to maintain the designation as a general-purpose AI model with systemic risk, providers may request reassessment at the earliest six months after that decision.
@ref Art 52(5) first sentence (src:781)
GIVEN `the date asked` IS A DATE
      `the model has been designated as a general-purpose AI model with systemic risk pursuant to paragraph 4` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the provider has made a reasoned request` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Art 52(5) the Commission must take the request into account` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT (`Art 51 the group applies on the date asked` `the date asked`)
            THEN NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): Chapter V applies from the date Art 113 gives
        IF NOT `the model has been designated as a general-purpose AI model with systemic risk pursuant to paragraph 4`
            THEN NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "a provider whose model has been designated as a general-purpose AI model with systemic risk pursuant to paragraph 4"
        IF `the provider has made a reasoned request`
            THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE JUST FALSE  -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Upon a reasoned request of a provider ..." ("upon" counts as "where": when no request is made the answer is no)

